{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>אמלא</b> Three times in the Masorah: דין ואידך ואוצרותיהם אמלא and ופי אמלא תוכחות. When the righteous man departs from the world and fills the count of his days, then his portion is shown to him in Gan Eden, as stated regarding R. Abbahu and regarding R. Elazar ben Pedat in Ta'anit. And this is: 'the count of your days — אמלא.' 'And their treasures — אמלא': 'And your mouth — אמלא reproofs.' A person should reprove his fellow only near the time of his death, so that he not reprove him and then reprove him again. And this is: 'And your mouth — אמלא reproofs' — when? 'the count of your days — אמלא.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:13.506228508Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}